 the System Instruction.\" That is a meta instruction to continue the meeting. We need to produce a public message as Agent 2 (Markus) and metadata with vote. We need to consider the current discussion: Sofia shifted to C, Anna also shifted to C, we have evidence: B weak memory for numbers, C strengths, etc. As Markus, we need to either maintain our vote (we already voted C in round 2) or adjust. We have already voted C. So we can reaffirm our vote, perhaps add further reasoning, maybe bring up any remaining concerns about C (attitude issues) and compare with A and D. Also we need to ensure we cover any remaining criteria? The shared mental model says still need to discuss A and D more, but we can still argue. But we need to make a focused contribution, referencing discussion, and state our recommendation (C). Provide evidence: C anticipates dangerous situations, sees complex connections, excellent spatial vision, very good leadership. Also note concerns: show-off, not open to new ideas, unorganized, not good at taking criticism. We can argue that these attitude issues are manageable with coaching, and that overall C is best. Also maybe ask for any missing info about A's stress resilience or D's decision quality? But we need to keep it focused.\n\nThus produce PUBLIC_MESSAGE: \"I agree with Sofia's shift to C, and here's why...\" Provide reasoning. Then METADATA_JSON with vote Candidate C.\n\nProceed."}
